Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Archipelagic Waters, version 4. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/629

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Territorial Seas (12NM), version 4. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/633

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Contiguous Zones (24NM), version 4. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/630

Flanders Marine Institute (2023). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: Maritime Boundaries and Exclusive Economic Zones (200NM), version 12. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/632

Flanders Marine Institute (2024). Maritime Boundaries Geodatabase: High Seas, version 2. Available online at https://www.marineregions.org/. https://doi.org/10.14284/696

Flanders Marine Institute (2020). World Countries Geodatabase. https://marineinfo.org/doc/dataset/8873

Land features (kind=land) use the updated World Countries Geodatabase from the Marine Regions WFS layer MarineRegions:worldcountries_esri_2014. This dataset adapts ESRI World Countries 2014, with source data from DeLorme (2014), to be consistent with Marine Regions maritime boundaries. Original source attribution: ESRI and DeLorme (2014), https://www.esri.com/. Country polygon rings are rounded to 1e-5 degrees, simplified at 0.0001° and split into short lines. They include inland borders and holes and are a proxy for normal baselines, not a complete legal-baseline model. Their upstream title, feature count and SHA-256 are recorded in upstream.lock.json. Marine Regions land_v9 is not used.

VLIZ has approved redistribution of the derived tiles. Maintainers monitor Marine Regions updates to avoid distributing deprecated versions. The permission scope and update process are recorded in CONTRIBUTING.md. This NOTICE describes the World Countries build; releases containing OpenStreetMap data retain their own NOTICE and ODbL 1.0 terms.
